# Run the sandbox

Task-focused recipes for the containerised agent sandbox. For *why* it exists
and what it isolates, see [The agent sandbox](../explanation/sandbox.md); for
services, ports, and env vars, see the [sandbox reference](../reference/sandbox.md).

## Start a session

```bash
# 1. Build the image (once, plus after editing docker/agent/Dockerfile)
just sandbox-build

# 2. Start the supporting services (searxng{% if sandbox_observability != 'none' %} + {{ sandbox_observability }}{% endif %}) in the background
just sandbox-up

# 3. Drop into the sandbox shell — your agent CLIs are available inside
just sandbox-shell
#   inside the container:
{%- if 'claude_code' in coding_agents %}
#     claude          # start Claude Code
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'codex' in coding_agents %}
#     codex           # start Codex CLI
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'aider' in coding_agents %}
#     aider           # start Aider
{%- endif %}
{%- if 'opencode' in coding_agents %}
#     opencode        # start OpenCode
{%- endif %}
#     just qa         # the quality gate runs identically here

# 4. Tear everything down (containers + networks; volumes stay)
just sandbox-down
```

`just sandbox-nuke` additionally removes the named volumes (caches, observability
data) — destructive, use when you want a clean slate.

## Populate the secrets in `.env`
{% if sandbox_auto_init %}
If `copier copy` ran with `--trust` and both `just` + `openssl` were on the PATH,
`.env` was already populated with random hex values during generation. If any of
those preconditions was missing, Copier printed a WARN and `.env` is unpopulated
— run it once now:

```bash
just sandbox-init
```

`just sandbox-init` is idempotent — already-set variables are skipped — so it's
safe to re-run to add a newly-introduced key. `.env` is git-ignored and never
committed.
{% else %}
Generate the missing secrets before the first `just sandbox-up`:

```bash
just sandbox-init        # idempotent; skips keys already set
```

Or set them by hand, e.g. `echo "SEARXNG_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env`.
`.env` is git-ignored and never committed. See the
[sandbox reference](../reference/sandbox.md#generated-secrets) for the full key list.
{% endif %}

## Forward a new environment variable

The agent shell only sees the env vars declared in `docker-compose.yml`. To add
one, declare it there explicitly and source it from your shell — **never**
hard-code a secret into the compose file or the image.
{%- if sandbox_observability == 'langfuse' %}

## First boot of Langfuse

`just sandbox-up` starts the Langfuse v3 stack at
`http://localhost:${LANGFUSE_PORT:-3000}`.
{% if sandbox_auto_init %}The auto-generated secrets are already in `.env` (or run `just sandbox-init`). Then:
{% else %}Set the required secrets in `.env` first (the compose file fails loudly on `:?`
guards if they're missing) — `just sandbox-init` generates them. Then:
{% endif %}
1. Open the UI and create an org + project.
2. Copy `LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY` and `LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY` from the project settings
   into `.env` — these are created after first login and cannot be auto-generated.
3. Restart so the new vars are forwarded: `just sandbox-down && just sandbox-up`.
{%- elif sandbox_observability == 'mlflow' %}

## Use MLflow

`just sandbox-up` starts an MLflow tracking server at
`http://localhost:${MLFLOW_PORT:-5000}`. Point your code at
`$MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI` (already forwarded into the sandbox shell) to log runs.
No first-login step is needed.
{%- endif %}

## Restrict network egress

The sandbox does not block outbound traffic (see
[the explanation](../explanation/sandbox.md#what-the-sandbox-does-not-isolate)).
On a corporate network, block egress from the sandbox CIDR (`172.28.0.0/16`) to
internal ranges:

```bash
# Linux (iptables)
sudo iptables -I DOCKER-USER -s 172.28.0.0/16 \
  -d 10.0.0.0/8,192.168.0.0/16,172.16.0.0/12 -j REJECT
sudo iptables -I DOCKER-USER -s 172.28.0.0/16 \
  -d 169.254.169.254/32 -j REJECT
```

```pf
# macOS (pf.conf)
block out quick from 172.28.0.0/16 to <rfc1918>
block out quick from 172.28.0.0/16 to 169.254.169.254
```
